---
import LandingPageShell from '../../layouts/LandingPageShell.astro'
---

<LandingPageShell
  title="Living Library"
  description="Real people. Real stories. Real conversations. Connect with someone whose life experience is different from yours and have meaningful conversation."
>
  <section class="landing-section landing-section--hero" aria-labelledby="landing-page-title">
    <div class="landing-panel">
      <p class="landing-eyebrow">Living Library</p>
      <h1 id="landing-page-title">A vertically scrolling landing shell is now in place.</h1>
      <p class="landing-lede">
        The homepage route now renders through reusable landing-page components
        instead of the old swipe deck, so the remaining sections can be built in
        thin slices.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="landing-section" aria-labelledby="landing-roadmap-title">
    <div class="landing-section-heading">
      <p class="landing-kicker">Scaffold</p>
      <h2 id="landing-roadmap-title">Section anchors are ready for the next stories.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="landing-grid">
      <article class="landing-card" id="how-it-works">
        <p class="landing-card__eyebrow">US-004 to US-010</p>
        <h3>How it works</h3>
        <p>
          The new page flow now has a stable place for the story explanation,
          participant quotes, and metrics content.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="landing-card" id="upcoming-sessions">
        <p class="landing-card__eyebrow">US-005 to US-007</p>
        <h3>Hero and sessions</h3>
        <p>
          The hero treatment, Instagram embed, and Luma session block can be
          added without reopening the route shell.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="landing-card" id="get-involved">
        <p class="landing-card__eyebrow">US-011 to US-012</p>
        <h3>Get involved and connect</h3>
        <p>
          The lower-page action cards, contact treatment, and footer can now
          land as isolated follow-up tasks.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</LandingPageShell>
